{"case_id":"C022","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":97,"change_types":["modified functionality","new state requirement","input-model expansion"],"affected_functions":["json_deep_copy","do_deep_copy","json_object_deep_copy","json_array_deep_copy","jsonp_loop_check"],"reason":"The commit changes json_deep_copy to track parent containers and reject circular object or array references, but the existing harness only parses bytes with json_loadb and serializes the resulting value with json_dumps or json_dump_callback. It never calls json_deep_copy, and parsed JSON alone cannot represent the in-memory circular graphs targeted by the new logic. A harness path that programmatically constructs container graphs and invokes json_deep_copy is therefore needed to test the changed functionality.","evidence":["H0 calls json_loadb followed only by json_dumps or json_dump_callback; it contains no call to json_deep_copy.","json_deep_copy now initializes a parents_set hashtable and delegates to do_deep_copy.","json_object_deep_copy and json_array_deep_copy now call jsonp_loop_check and propagate failures from recursive copying.","The new behavior concerns circular references between in-memory json_t containers, while H0 derives its json_t exclusively from serialized JSON input."],"recommended_action":"Extend the harness, or add a dedicated target, that uses fuzz-controlled data to build object and array graphs—including self-references, mutual cycles, shared acyclic children, and ordinary nested values—and calls json_deep_copy while correctly releasing all created values."}
